Brief Review of Lecture: Control Flow
If / Else = Conditional Behavior
if (x &gt; 0) {
  print("positive")
} else {
  print("not positive")
}
Vectorized If/Else statements are also possible:

x = 0
ifelse(test = x &lt; 0, yes = "is positive :)", no = "is negative :(")



[1] "is negative :("


For loops = repeat over items
for (i in 1:5) {
  print(i^2)
}

Brief Review of Lecture: Functions

